            <ArticleTitle>The psychodynamics of coronary heart rehabilitation: some basic understandings for allied health professionals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper details some of the patient's psychological factors with which each allied health professional must deal when interacting with an ill person. Successful professional/patient intervention is heavily dependent on a sensitivity to these factors. Within this framework, this paper deals with the personality dynamics which facilitate the effective rehabilitation of patients in general, but coronary heart disease patients in particular.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
